{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1534936-what-are-the-bogatyri","id":1534936,"title":"What are the Bogatyri?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-04-30T04:24:26-07:00","id":1534936,"title":"What are the Bogatyri?","content":"Or what could be the <b>Bogatyri, </b>considering we never had a proper answer to this one<br /> I'm curious of your ideas!<br /> <br /> So what we know:<br /> - The bogatyri (singular bogatyr) were personal guardians of the the Eldest<br /> - According Yorak -who know a thing or two - the bogatyri <i>were not</i> kine, Lupine, or Cainite.<br /> - Although they appeared mortal, they claimed lineage from Meru, a mystical mountain in India and supposed birthplace of the Arioi (what occult-scholars would later call the mythical Aryan race).<br /> (Worth tho mention, Meru was the mythical seat of the Wan Xian, their most holy site; it was a temple complex that served as the headquarter of the Wan Xian, right under the sight of the August Personage of Jade. Here, the rogue immortals turned on their own children, the Jin Hai, an act that finally caused their cursing. According the Kuei-jin, Meru was located on the Tibetan plateau.<br /> The Chi\u2019n Ta believe that Mount Kailas is the remnant of Meru and that the Searing Wind attempted to take it with the aid of a corrupted Wu Lung, which sparked the Dragon River War.<br /> The Fera tell an entirely different story: According to them, Meru is the remnant of Toba, a supervulcano that erupted in Prehistory and unleashed the Banestorm. Toba lies in what is now a lake in Sumatra, meaning that the Wan Xian would originate south, not from the west of the Middle Kingdom)<br /> - Metal refused to cut their unblemished skin, while stone and wood forswore never to bruise them. (This is something VERY interesting and not unlike the Pact the True Fae in Changeling the Lost made with the elements of the word, except Iron who they pissed off... and a bit like Baldr, her mother took an oath from fire and water, iron and all metals, stones and earth, from trees, sicknesses and poisons, and from all four-footed beasts, birds and creeping things, that they would not hurt her son, but forgot the humble and a bit dumb mistletoe)<br /> - The bogatyri came into the Eldest's service when the Deluge washed a band of them against the Carpathians. In return for the Eldest's hospitality and-succor, they offered their allegiance<br /> - Each bogatyr possessed a skin pouch holding the flesh of the Antediluvian - when they fought for it, the skin pouch crawled over their faces and gave them the countenance of the Eldest. Their forearm bones extended into blades, while their tongues darted out like daggers.<br /> \u200b- When the Eldest fell to Samiel, the bogatyri scattered to the four winds to find it. They never returned, even after Yorak sent them messages that the Dracon had carried the Eldest embrionic form<br /> - Lambach Ruthven believes the bogatyri split and now guard the different manifestations of the Eldest. He claim he seen two under New York<br /> <br /> So... this is not that much<br /> They are an old race, that is for sure, existed before the Flood and survived it<br /> They appeared mortal but probably they were not<br /> They had strong mystical connections, matal, stone and wood outright refused to hurt them<br /> It is debatable if the ability to extended theirforearm into blades, like Barakka from Mortal Kombat, while their tongues darted out like daggers is a natural trait or the gift of the Eldest<br /> <br /> The word bogatyr is not of Slavic origin It derives from the Turco-Mongolic baghatur &quot;hero&quot;, which is itself of uncertain origin. The term is recorded from at least the 8th century.<br /> In folklore, the bylinas (b<i>ylinas and starinas about bogatyrs and wizards, fairy tales and ritual lamentations \u2013 for a long time a whole cultural layer of the Old Russian song tradition remained alive in local villages</i>) mention dozens of different Russian bogatyrs. Tales about bogatyrs, the strong men of the distant past, are among every Russian boy and girl\u2019s favorite bedtime stories.<br /> There are three elder bogatyrs: Svyatogor, Volga Svyatoslavich and Mikula Selyaninovich.<br /> Svyatogor is the oldest and strongest bogatyr. Historians and philologists agree that Svyatogor is most probably a pre-Christian hero of Russian lore. Svyatogor is a <b>huge giant</b> who lives in the Holy mountains. When he walks, Mother Earth shakes, forests sway and rivers overflow their banks. Various bylinas tell that Svyatogor is either trapped in the earth (after trying to lift all the Earth\u2019s weight collected in a bag) or immobilized in a stone coffin. In any case, Svyatogor is a personification of some ancient all-encompassing power. He\u2019s too strong and too heavy for Earth to carry him.<br /> \u200bVolga Svyatoslavich is another pre-Christian bogatyr. His mother was a princess and his father was a magical serpent, hence Volga\u2019s ability to transform himself into various creatures and understand the language of animals. There are many tales about Volga\u2019s conquest of the foreign lands, Indian or Turkish.<br /> Mikula Selyaninovich is the ultimate peasant bogatyr. His patronymic, Selyaninovich, means \u2018son of a villager\u2019 and he\u2019s invincible, because \u201cmother Earth loves his kin\u201d. It is Mikula who gives Svyatogor a bag with all the Earth\u2019s weight, that Svyatogor can\u2019t lift.<br /> All the other bogatyrs are considered to be \u201cjunior\u201d bogatyrs. There are dozens of them in the byliny and, frankly speaking, most Russian people don\u2019t remember them by now.<br /> Though not as heavily researched, the female bogatyr or polianitsa is a female warrior akin to the Amazons. While the female bogatyr doesn't quite match the men in strength and bravery, there are stories detailing instances where they save their husbands and outwit the enemy<br /> <br /> What do you think, what are the Bogatyri?<br /> Or what could be?<br /> Ever used one of these powerhouses? Even in modern nights something that immune wood, metal and stone is a formidable opponent...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-30T15:06:50-07:00","id":1534963,"title":"","content":"I never cared about the concept of the Bogatyri so they simply don't exist in my chronicles. They don't seem interesting to me. I don't think they add anything to the game that I like. In so far that their legend may exist, it's just more bullshit spouted by Tzimisce elders to make them and their creator seem more spooky and terrifying to the other clans.<br /> <br /> For some reason, the writers of the Revised era really, really liked the Tzimisce Antedeluvian so they created a lot of superfluous backstory for it. None of it interested me because quite frankly I've never liked the Tzimisce all that much. I never thought Vicissitude was that interesting, and in fact was counter to a game of gothic horror vampires. For years I wondered why this was even in the game until I finally discovered it was an attempt to emulate Necroscope style vampires. I still didn't like it, but at least I now understand why it was put in a game. Since I don't like Necroscope's conception of vampires, it was enough for me to decide to remove that Discipline entirely, give Protean to the Tzimisce, and adjust the setting accordingly. So that the Sabbat could still create the bizarre Sczlachta and Vozhd on occasion, I gave some Sabbat Tzimisce access to Bio-Thaumaturgy to create these Dr Frankenstein creations. Works good enough for me.<br /> <br /> I think the original details we were given about the Tzimisce Antedeluvian in 2e was more than sufficient for any ST. From the Lugoj entry in Children of the Inquisition we learned that Tzimisce had survived. From the Zantosa entry in the Storytellers Guide to the Sabbat we learned that family of Revenants were hiding the torpored body of the antedeluvian. That's more than sufficient for the ST to dream up plots if he wanted. I don't think all the other details we've been given make this vampire any more interesting, or make me want to use him more than any other antedeluvian.<br /> <br /> In so far that I use the actual bylinas and folklore figures in my chronicle, I treat the bogatyrs as I do most legendary heroes - they are most likely Mages of a now discontinued &quot;heroic&quot; Tradition that slew monsters and performed impossible deeds, using their Spheres to augment their bodies. Perhaps focusing on the Life sphere. The Bogatyrs, Beowulf, the Greek demigods, Melqart, the heroes of the Shahnameh, some of the Knights of the Round Table, etc. are all part of that. Those who aren't actually Garou that is or Mages of another tradition.<br /> <br /> I reject a lot of the - let's call it unique - contributions of the Revised era. What scratched their itch never did anything for me. So while there are some elements I used, I've created a lot of my own elements or built on certain things introduced earlier that weren't developed.<br /> <br /> I know it's not too helpful to you! So hoping you can get other posts that build on your interests.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-30T15:34:06-07:00","id":1534968,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1534936-what-are-the-bogatyri#post1534936\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">O<br /> The Chi\u2019n Ta</div> </div> </div> </div>That's an aspirant mark. It applies to the letter just before it. The problem: You can't aspirate vowels.<br /> <br /> (Yes, I know it's the text's fault. I still hate it, and it doesn't mean what WW wanted it to mean.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-30T16:10:54-07:00","id":1534970,"title":"","content":"A friend of mine who read the Revised Tzimisce clan book when it first came out in the early 2000s said he thought the Bogatyri were Exalted, probably Dragon-Blooded.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-30T16:37:11-07:00","id":1534972,"title":"","content":"If not Mages, I think the Bogatyrs could be Changelings, if they're still alive. Keeping in mind that I thoroughly ignore the DA fae and instead use the normal Changeling rules with just a little tweaking.<br /> <br /> Changelings deal with vampires amicably, have superhuman Birthrights and magic that could very well translate into the legends of such heroes. Heck, they fight actual dragons and whatnot even today. And they also do offer their services through Oaths.<br /> <br /> Other than that, I have mostly the same opinion as <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3046_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3046\" data-vbnamecard=\"3046\">Black Fox</a>, just less intense, except I kinda like Vicissitude.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-01T03:25:00-07:00","id":1534992,"title":"","content":"Since Mt. Meru pops up in multiple cultures, there are quite a few options. If we take bogatyr as a sobriquet assigned to them in the slavic area, Wan Xian fit rather well as the heroic type - only, that doesn't really vibe with the character of the Eldest, imo. If they are paladins, I see them more as 'awful good' rather than 'lawful good'.<br /> Meru is also the home of Devas and Asuras, the latter of which would fit better. There are types of Asuras that can change their shape, which would fit with the quasi-Vicissitude. The elemental immunity on the other hand makes it sound more like a Taoist thing, with them being something like offspring of the Heavenly Beasts.<br /> <br /> In all cases that would make them some kind of demigod, so <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar26996_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"26996\" data-vbnamecard=\"26996\">Amethyst</a>'s friend may actually be on to something with Exalted, considering the cross-over attempts between WOD and AOS some supplements made. Mechanically, I think they would make sense as the product of something ephemeral (Umbrood) and mortal. Hard to tell which one exactly.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-01T07:36:03-07:00","id":1535002,"title":"","content":"The Exalted idea might be very appropriate but, if one opts not to have crossovers with it, I think my likely choice would be some unique remnant of the Wan Xian. They are corrupted (whether from before serving the Eldest or because of it), but they were so powerful that they can't be simply put in the same category as the Kuei-jin.<br /> <br /> The idea of them being Fae from Changeling also intrigues me, but I'm too uninformed about that splat to evaluate this option properly.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-05T06:25:46-07:00","id":1535169,"title":"","content":"I can't claim to have ever used the Bogatyri in any game I've ever done but I would say that if I ever ran with them, then keeping them mysterious would be a major part. The idea of them guarding different parts of [Tzimisce] scattered all over the place is something which sounds pretty good to me. It would for one thing explain why they don't just steamroll any and all threats to said Ancient.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-05T13:18:26-07:00","id":1535183,"title":"","content":"I just haven't used them cuz I don't find a good use. But I do find them interesting! <br /> Thing is, not even Transylvania Chronicles use them, which would've been the right place for it.<br /> <br /> The changeling/fae idea is mostly my favorite. <br /> For their relationship with the Eldest is much like that of a millenary pact. But I think it would've been better if we got a set number of them, and where they are.<br /> <br /> Like, there is a thread about all the pieces of the Eldest. All in all we got Vykos (dracon, illias and eldest inside them until it was supposedly removed), the amorphous thing that was in NY, the tree in the haven of Damek Ruthven, and Lugoj (and maybe on other people who took part in the diablerie of the Eldest in case you didn't follow the metaplot strictly).<br /> I don't know about the other (except the 2 at NY), but I'm certain the Bogatyri are keeping Lugoj.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Strange... When coincidence seems too convenient, I prefer to call it fate.</i><br /> <br /> <b><sup>-Blood Omen: Legacy of Kain</sup> </b>d=","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25534-banu_saulot","name":"Banu_Saulot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25534_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-05T18:35:40-07:00","id":1535186,"title":"","content":"I think that keeping the number unsaid is better as a way to let storytellers make what's best for a given chronicle. Joting down the number and identity of the pieces is easy to do for an individual Storyteller, while it is more work than it is worth it as world building.<br /> <br /> Basically, while the idea that the Ancient exists in pieces is cool and entertaining, a fixed list of such pieces doesn't add anything else to the game as a whole.<br /> <br /> At most we need what that thread already gave: a list of main suspects.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-11T11:39:00-07:00","id":1535451,"title":"","content":"That is a serious problem with WoD<br /> Just creates secret boxes, like JJ Abrams and leaves the rest in the hands of the Storyteller.<br /> Generally not giving an inch of content for them to choose between. Just the idea of a secret possibility and considering a job well done.<br /> <br /> Not giving content should not be applauded, that was a pain in the ass. Leave to the Storyteller to choose if they want to use content or not. WoD is not a show or book series for us to just speculate, it is supposed to be a game people run and have to build based on their material, but is not the work of the storyteller to create everything. Otherwise the tons of books would be useless.<br /> <br /> This ethos of 'here is this idea' and 'no, I've gave you the idea, do all the rest of the work', then dress it as giving power to the storyteller and being inspirational was really detrimental to the setting and the game in my opinion. Specially when there were things we really couldn't want less to have confirmed (like Antediluvians existing in all their might), and they did it anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Strange... When coincidence seems too convenient, I prefer to call it fate.</i><br /> <br /> <b><sup>-Blood Omen: Legacy of Kain</sup> </b>d=","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25534-banu_saulot","name":"Banu_Saulot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25534_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-07T22:43:33-07:00","id":1536929,"title":"","content":"&quot;I never thought Vicissitude was that interesting, and in fact was counter to a game of gothic horror vampires.&quot;<br /> <br /> Me either. It reeked of someone who liked the &quot;Necroscope&quot; vampires, and The Thing. It should have been relegated as a trans-dimensional virus that should be exterminated. It's an extemely overpowered &quot;Discipline,&quot; and it's a good thing that's it's been demoted as a variation of Protean. And it's effects should always be temporary, except for level 10 &quot;Plot Device.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25666-illuminostro","name":"Illuminostro","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"166"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}